The open-world city builder, skinned people and their procedural animation, the AI, the mission system, the dialogue and the stand-in sounds were written for this game. Voices use the text-to-speech voices installed on the player's own computer.

[b]Textures, faces, interface and city[/b]
Every texture, face, SVG interface element and building is generated by code written for this game (tools/). No outside art assets are used. The city layout follows S M Nazmuz Sakib's own reference photographs of Sontek, Dania and Jatrabari.

[b]Exam papers[/b]
Questions are paraphrased from public question papers of the Bangladesh Public Service Commission (BCS preliminary examinations), the Directorate of Primary Education (Assistant Teacher recruitment), the Bangladesh Road Transport Authority (Motor Vehicle Inspector recruitment) and the Bangladesh Bar Council (advocates' enrolment examinations). Answers were checked against the LiveMCQ and Satt Academy solution pages. None of these bodies has endorsed this game.
The other 2,500+ questions are original practice questions written for this game in the style of those exams (tools/generate_questions.py). They are not past-paper questions; each one records the fact table or calculation it was built from.

[b]Places[/b]
Real streets, Dania College and Jurain Graveyard appear by name as places. Every business, mosque, school, character and organisation in the story is fictional.
